# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp

# Runtime state & generated output — kept out of the repo so your company's
# data (org config, deliverables, generated agent bios) isn't published.
# A fresh clone boots with an empty org from the app's built-in defaults.
data-bureau.json
data-foreman.json
data-*.backup-*.json
data-bureau-ws-*.json
data-bureau-workspaces.json
drafts/
drafts-*/
agent-profiles/
agent-profiles-*/

# The dead-man's switch's ping URL. A healthchecks-style ping URL is a BEARER SECRET: anyone holding it
# can forge liveness, which means the alarm you are relying on goes quiet without ever firing. The tools
# (tools/heartbeat.mjs, Install-Heartbeat.ps1) are tracked; the URL they read is not.
heartbeat.local.json

# Prototype / scratch pages
public/_*.html

# session backups + sqlite db
_backup-*/
data-bureau.db
data-bureau.db-*

# detached-server runtime logs (from launching `node server.mjs` in the background)
server.out.log
server.err.log

# eval harness: timestamped run reports (the committed baseline.json is the tracked reference)
eval/reports/

# Start-Bureau.ps1's detached-mode logs
bureau.log
bureau.log.err

# The rotating in-process log (server.mjs tees stdout/stderr), the boot task's stream 2/6 capture, and
# the daily backup's output. The GLOB is the point: `bureau.log` was already listed above, but every
# rotated generation — bureau.log.1, .2, .3 — was still tracked, as were boot.log and backup.log.
# These carry objectives, agent output and error traces, so publishing them publishes the workspace.
*.log
*.log.[0-9]
# ...and the stderr sibling of any of them. `bureau.log.err` is named above, but the launcher's boot
# capture was split into its OWN file on 2026-08-18 and the rename carried its stderr file along:
# bureau.boot.log.err matched none of the patterns here, so it showed up untracked the next time
# anyone ran `git status`. A glob, so the next such rename does not repeat it.
*.log.err
